## Original Content
L’entrée dans la course à l’Élysée de Raphaël Glucksmann dans le cadre de la primaire socialiste, peut-être bientôt suivie par celles d’Olivier Faure et de Boris Vallaud, et par la candidature hors primaire du communiste Fabien Roussel illustrent la difficulté de s’y retrouver face à la pléthore de candidatures à gauche. France 24 fait le point.

## Summary
The article discusses the entry of Raphaël Glucksmann into the French presidential race through the Socialist Party primary, with potential follow-ups from Olivier Faure and Boris Vallaud, and the non-primary candidacy of Communist Fabien Roussel, highlighting the difficulty caused by numerous left-wing candidates. France 24 provides an overview of this political situation.

## Key Points
- Raphaël Glucksmann is entering the presidential race via the Socialist Party primary.
- Olivier Faure and Boris Vallaud may also join the race as Socialist candidates.
- Fabien Roussel is running independently outside the primary as a communist candidate.
- The proliferation of left-wing candidates creates confusion and challenges for the political left.
- France 24 is reporting on the issues surrounding multiple candidacies.


